# =============================================================================
# Store — LIST requests (VS Code REST Client) — GET /api/v1/stores (ADMIN)
# =============================================================================
# Semantics (ticket 0010, Q2): the list is OPERATIONAL TRUTH, not an audit
# log — CLOSED stores are hidden; ACTIVE/PENDING/BLOCKED all stay visible
# (pending and blocked are alive, just not trading). Request 10 proves the
# hiding live: a store that was in the list vanishes after it is closed.
#
# How to run:
#   1. Start the backend: `docker compose up -d --build` — http://localhost:4000
#   2. Click the "Send Request" CodeLens above any request, IN ORDER, in one
#      sitting (captures are session-scoped).
#
# Prerequisites: the admin persona (see http/store/delete.http header for
# the SQL promotion one-liner).
#
# Notes:
#   - All data is FAKE (devtunde.com emails, Nigerian numbers).
#   - The automated suite for these endpoints: StoreApiTests (src/test/java).
#   - Re-runnable: both manager personas, both brands and contact emails are
#     minted fresh each run with {{$timestamp}} — no 409 collisions with
#     prior runs.
#   - Access tokens expire after 15 MINUTES. If tokened requests suddenly 401,
#     re-send the SETUP requests from the top (they mint and re-capture).
#   - REST Client captures die on file/VS Code reopen. If you see raw {{...}}
#     template text being sent or sudden 500s, re-send the setup requests
#     from the top — never continue on a dead capture.
#   - Expected codes: 200 list (array of LIVE stores), 401 no/invalid token,
#     403 non-admin, 405 wrong method, 404 trailing slash, 204 close.
# =============================================================================

@storeUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/stores
@authUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth

### 1 — Setup: login the admin persona
# Expected: 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2 — Setup: signup manager A (minted fresh each run)
# Expected: 201
# @name sellerASignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Stay Open Manager",
  "email": "probe-list-a-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234586"
}

### 3 — Setup: login manager A
# Expected: 200
# @name sellerALogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{sellerASignup.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 4 — Setup: signup manager B (minted fresh each run)
# Expected: 201
# @name sellerBSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Doomed Manager",
  "email": "probe-list-b-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234587"
}

### 5 — Setup: login manager B
# Expected: 200
# @name sellerBLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{sellerBSignup.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 6 — Setup: create the store that will STAY open (minted brand)
# Expected: 201
# @name storeOpen
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Probe Open Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{sellerALogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "12 Market Road, Lagos",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "probe-open-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 7 — Setup: create the store that will be CLOSED (minted brand)
# Expected: 201
# @name storeClosed
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Probe Closed Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "KIOSK",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{sellerBLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "45 New Address, Ikeja",
    "phone": "08087654321",
    "email": "probe-will-close-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 8 — List BEFORE closing
# Expected: 200 — array contains BOTH minted brands ("Probe Open Store ..." and
# "Probe Closed Store ..."). Eyeball it — both are alive right now
GET {{storeUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 9 — Close the second store
# Expected: 204
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/{{storeClosed.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 10 — List AFTER closing
# Expected: 200 — "Probe Open Store ..." is STILL THERE; "Probe Closed
# Store ..." is GONE (CLOSED hidden — Q2). The closed row survives at the DB
# level; the list is operational truth, not an audit log
GET {{storeUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 11 — No Authorization header
# Expected: 401
GET {{storeUrl}}

### 12 — Garbage token
# Expected: 401
GET {{storeUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-jwt

### 13 — Setup: signup the regular persona (fixed — she never holds a seat)
# Expected: 201 (409 if she already exists — either way the account exists)
# @name regularSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Bola Listless",
  "email": "bola.listless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234588"
}

### 14 — Setup: login the regular persona
# Expected: 200
# @name regularLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bola.listless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 15 — List as a regular user
# Expected: 403 — the collection is admin-only
GET {{storeUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{regularLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 16 — Wrong method: DELETE against the collection
# Expected: 405 — Allow: GET, POST
DELETE {{storeUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 17 — Wrong method: PUT against the collection
# Expected: 405 — Allow: GET, POST
PUT {{storeUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 18 — Trailing slash
# Expected: 404 — Spring 7 / Boot 4 does not do trailing-slash matching
GET {{storeUrl}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 19 — HEAD against the collection
# Expected: 200 — Spring auto-supports HEAD for GET routes (empty body)
HEAD {{storeUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
